WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.166 --> 00:00:08.593
- [Interviewer] All right, Flakah.

00:00:08.593 --> 00:00:09.426
- Yes.

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:10.418
- [Interviewer] Flakah,
where'd you grow up?

00:00:10.418 --> 00:00:11.505
Where are you from originally?

00:00:11.505 --> 00:00:13.873
- [Flakah] I grew up in Long Beach.

00:00:13.873 --> 00:00:14.706
- [Interviewer] And tell
me about your family.

00:00:14.706 --> 00:00:16.029
You had both of your
parents when you were a kid?

00:00:16.029 --> 00:00:16.987
- No.

00:00:16.987 --> 00:00:20.798
Grew up with my mother and a stepfather.

00:00:20.798 --> 00:00:22.652
He's actually been in our lives

00:00:22.652 --> 00:00:25.448
for since I was a little girl.

00:00:25.448 --> 00:00:30.253
But before that, it was just
like random ass guys, you know?

00:00:30.253 --> 00:00:31.503
Typical shit your parents do,

00:00:31.503 --> 00:00:33.574
leave you at home type shit or whatever.

00:00:33.574 --> 00:00:35.023
- [Interviewer] And
how was your childhood?

00:00:35.023 --> 00:00:37.389
- It was pretty fucked up.

00:00:37.389 --> 00:00:38.353
For whatever reason,

00:00:38.353 --> 00:00:41.345
I was always being attacked by my mother.

00:00:41.345 --> 00:00:42.423
We never really got along.

00:00:42.423 --> 00:00:44.142
It was always just, you know,

00:00:44.142 --> 00:00:46.619
whatever happened in the
household with another sibling,

00:00:46.619 --> 00:00:47.519
it was always my fault.

00:00:47.519 --> 00:00:51.852
And you know, it was just,
it was kind of fucked up.

00:00:53.781 --> 00:00:56.174
And then that's when she got my stepdad

00:00:56.174 --> 00:00:58.206
and they used to get,

00:00:58.206 --> 00:01:01.021
well, they used to party
every weekend, you know?

00:01:01.021 --> 00:01:02.856
Leave Friday, whatever,

00:01:02.856 --> 00:01:05.401
party all night 'til Sunday, come home.

00:01:05.401 --> 00:01:07.401
Sleep all day on Sunday.

00:01:10.413 --> 00:01:11.761
And at that time,

00:01:11.761 --> 00:01:14.464
I probably was like in
like the fourth grade,

00:01:14.464 --> 00:01:17.024
maybe third or fourth grade.

00:01:17.024 --> 00:01:19.628
And they had a friend that
used to come over with them

00:01:19.628 --> 00:01:24.128
and he pretty much just tried
to take advantage of me.

00:01:25.561 --> 00:01:28.037
You know, I had my clothes down.

00:01:28.037 --> 00:01:29.999
He was trying to like
offer me money to like--

00:01:29.999 --> 00:01:30.905
- [Interviewer] And how old were you?

00:01:30.905 --> 00:01:31.738
- I was young.

00:01:31.738 --> 00:01:33.189
I was like six or seven,
somewhere around there.

00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:34.368
Like between those ages.

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:35.201
I'm not really sure.

00:01:35.201 --> 00:01:37.054
I don't remember.

00:01:37.054 --> 00:01:39.912
But I remember I was scared
and I told my cousin.

00:01:39.912 --> 00:01:41.337
And she's like, "You gotta tell your mom."

00:01:41.337 --> 00:01:43.423
And I was like, you know,

00:01:43.423 --> 00:01:45.612
it wasn't one of those
things where, you know,

00:01:45.612 --> 00:01:47.177
you can go tell your mom like,

00:01:47.177 --> 00:01:48.668
look, this is happening to me you know?

00:01:48.668 --> 00:01:52.550
And so I kept it to myself
until it happened to my cousin

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.657
and then she told my mom.

00:01:53.657 --> 00:01:54.490
And then she was like,

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:57.327
yeah, he did it to Flakah too or whatever.

00:01:57.327 --> 00:01:59.590
And then I got in trouble.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:00.423
I got in trouble.

00:02:00.423 --> 00:02:02.050
So like, you know, when you're that small,

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.707
you don't know what fuck's going on.

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:06.973
You don't know why shit is happening.

00:02:06.973 --> 00:02:07.806
You know?

00:02:07.806 --> 00:02:09.237
And if somebody else is touching on you

00:02:09.237 --> 00:02:11.887
and the one person who was
supposed to be protecting you

00:02:11.887 --> 00:02:14.077
like talks shit to you and yells at you

00:02:14.077 --> 00:02:15.717
because you didn't say shit

00:02:15.717 --> 00:02:17.812
instead of actually protecting you,

00:02:17.812 --> 00:02:20.288
it's like it kind of
puts a wall up for you.

00:02:20.288 --> 00:02:25.288
So, you know, like that's
kind of how it all started.

00:02:25.413 --> 00:02:26.768
I started drinking at nine,

00:02:26.768 --> 00:02:29.403
started smoking weed at nine.

00:02:29.403 --> 00:02:30.870
My mother had came.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.477
She moved and she left me

00:02:32.477 --> 00:02:33.778
and my brother with my grandmother,

00:02:33.778 --> 00:02:36.697
so we kinda just did whatever we want.

00:02:36.697 --> 00:02:38.818
You know, I'm like my grandma's favorite,

00:02:38.818 --> 00:02:40.444
so she never questioned anything I did,

00:02:40.444 --> 00:02:43.068
anywhere I went, who I was around.

00:02:43.068 --> 00:02:44.948
And that's kind of where
everything started.

00:02:44.948 --> 00:02:47.108
- [Instructor] So your mom was into drugs?

00:02:47.108 --> 00:02:47.941
- Yeah.

00:02:47.941 --> 00:02:49.613
She won't admit it,
but she was into drugs.

00:02:49.613 --> 00:02:52.147
Like she wasn't a full on addict.

00:02:52.147 --> 00:02:54.527
You know, she was like a
functional addict here and there,

00:02:54.527 --> 00:02:58.895
but she learned how to stop
or however she did it, but.

00:02:58.895 --> 00:02:59.905
- [Interviewer] And your dad?

00:02:59.905 --> 00:03:02.154
- My dad was a full-blown
addict, a full-blown.

00:03:02.154 --> 00:03:04.037
I used to get high with my dad.

00:03:04.037 --> 00:03:07.288
Well, my stepdad, but I call him my dad.

00:03:07.288 --> 00:03:09.268
But when we moved to Long Beach,

00:03:09.268 --> 00:03:11.217
that's when like kind of
everything just started,

00:03:11.217 --> 00:03:13.584
like started hanging around
with different people,

00:03:13.584 --> 00:03:16.508
getting into trouble, fights.

00:03:16.508 --> 00:03:17.978
I didn't really care, you know?

00:03:17.978 --> 00:03:20.498
Like I had a mother who was more involved

00:03:20.498 --> 00:03:22.718
with her dude than her kids.

00:03:22.718 --> 00:03:26.513
And then my stepdad had kids
and he has a lot of kids,

00:03:26.513 --> 00:03:28.359
so it was like a bunch
of us all, you know.

00:03:28.359 --> 00:03:30.257
At one point, it was all
of us in one household

00:03:30.257 --> 00:03:32.247
and it was just chaotic.

00:03:32.247 --> 00:03:34.087
I used to come home high every day.

00:03:34.087 --> 00:03:34.920
My mother never knew.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:35.753
My stepdad never knew

00:03:35.753 --> 00:03:36.830
'cause I would just go
straight to the room

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.252
and just block everything out.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.197
I was always in trouble.

00:03:40.197 --> 00:03:41.697
I was always grounded.

00:03:41.697 --> 00:03:43.961
If I answered the door when I was grounded

00:03:43.961 --> 00:03:45.257
and my parents walk in,

00:03:45.257 --> 00:03:47.339
I'm grounded again for being at the door.

00:03:47.339 --> 00:03:48.619
You know, it's just like
little shit like that.

00:03:48.619 --> 00:03:49.675
It's like as a little girl,

00:03:49.675 --> 00:03:51.628
it's like, what the fuck am I doing wrong?

00:03:51.628 --> 00:03:52.637
Like, what is it?

00:03:52.637 --> 00:03:54.272
Like, what's going on, you know?

00:03:54.272 --> 00:03:57.174
But it's like back in
the days, you don't talk.

00:03:57.174 --> 00:04:00.018
Like, parents don't talk to
their kids like that, you know?

00:04:00.018 --> 00:04:01.880
There's no DCFS or this,

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.893
like how they have all these rules now.

00:04:03.893 --> 00:04:05.727
So it's like everything just
gets swept under the carpet

00:04:05.727 --> 00:04:08.881
and you just keep on moving.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.214
So I left at 14,

00:04:12.249 --> 00:04:15.084
got with my first baby's dad,

00:04:15.084 --> 00:04:16.667
got pregnant at 15.

00:04:17.649 --> 00:04:18.959
That was (indistinct).

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:21.860
That was just like a whole
'nother life right there.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.277
Just being pregnant at 15 is,

00:04:25.455 --> 00:04:27.956
I mean, it's a scary ass thing, you know?

00:04:27.956 --> 00:04:29.499
I got kicked out of
school for being pregnant

00:04:29.499 --> 00:04:30.332
because they were scared

00:04:30.332 --> 00:04:34.053
that I was gonna influence the
other girls to be pregnant.

00:04:34.053 --> 00:04:35.870
So I spent a little time out,

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:36.980
like, you know, not going to school.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:39.590
Then I found a school where
I can go while I'm pregnant

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.809
and also have my kid there.

00:04:41.809 --> 00:04:44.464
So I started doing that.

00:04:44.464 --> 00:04:46.659
My baby's dad was into gangs,

00:04:46.659 --> 00:04:49.954
so by the time my son was like two months,

00:04:49.954 --> 00:04:52.639
he went to jail for 20 years.

00:04:52.639 --> 00:04:54.070
So I raised my son on my own.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:55.239
For like the first year or two,

00:04:55.239 --> 00:04:56.539
I was working, I was going to school.

00:04:56.539 --> 00:04:59.635
I was doing my internship for RN.

00:04:59.635 --> 00:05:01.864
You know, I was on my shit,

00:05:01.864 --> 00:05:04.109
but I was still partying every weekend,

00:05:04.109 --> 00:05:05.510
still drinking every weekend.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.529
Always had my son.

00:05:06.529 --> 00:05:08.885
Never neglected him, never did nothing.

00:05:08.885 --> 00:05:10.506
You know, he was always G'd up.

00:05:10.506 --> 00:05:12.095
Like I never, you know?

00:05:12.095 --> 00:05:14.314
I was a really mean mother.

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.888
Everything was not pretty and shit,

00:05:16.888 --> 00:05:20.069
but that's when I met my second baby's dad

00:05:20.069 --> 00:05:24.035
and that's where like
everything just went to shit.

00:05:24.035 --> 00:05:25.785
I have four kids now.

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:31.192
From the moment I had my first daughter,

00:05:31.192 --> 00:05:33.946
that's when I started using meth.

00:05:33.946 --> 00:05:36.542
And it was just an everyday thing,

00:05:36.542 --> 00:05:38.224
an everyday all day thing.

00:05:38.224 --> 00:05:39.901
House was always dirty.

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:40.852
You know, the kids were fed,

00:05:40.852 --> 00:05:41.851
they went to school and all that,

00:05:41.851 --> 00:05:45.312
but it was a whole 'nother side of neglect

00:05:45.312 --> 00:05:46.407
for the kids, you know?

00:05:46.407 --> 00:05:48.708
Shit that I experienced as a child

00:05:48.708 --> 00:05:51.352
that I never wanted to bring to my kids.

00:05:51.352 --> 00:05:52.477
And it's exactly what I did

00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:54.461
and I did it 10 times worse.

00:05:54.461 --> 00:05:57.128
So that went on for a few years.

00:05:58.102 --> 00:06:01.877
The whole DCFS got
involved, lost the kids,

00:06:01.877 --> 00:06:04.913
got them back, lost them again.

00:06:04.913 --> 00:06:07.181
Just, I mean, I don't know.

00:06:07.181 --> 00:06:08.913
It's just been chaos.

00:06:08.913 --> 00:06:10.183
It's been chaos.

00:06:10.183 --> 00:06:13.051
You know, going in and out of jail.

00:06:13.051 --> 00:06:15.471
Using dope, selling dope,

00:06:15.471 --> 00:06:18.930
doing all kinds of illegal activities

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.641
that I will not repeat, but--

00:06:20.641 --> 00:06:21.891
- [Interviewer] So you
joined a gang eventually?

00:06:21.891 --> 00:06:23.138
- [Flakah] No, I never joined the gang.

00:06:23.138 --> 00:06:23.971
I never joined.

00:06:23.971 --> 00:06:26.032
I was always the type to,

00:06:26.032 --> 00:06:27.141
I'm always against authority,

00:06:27.141 --> 00:06:28.363
so like even in a gang,

00:06:28.363 --> 00:06:29.265
it's like you have rules.

00:06:29.265 --> 00:06:31.052
You have certain places you can't go,

00:06:31.052 --> 00:06:32.841
certain people you can't talk to.

00:06:32.841 --> 00:06:34.244
And I'm just everywhere.

00:06:34.244 --> 00:06:35.082
I don't care.

00:06:35.082 --> 00:06:36.382
I'll talk to whoever, you know?

00:06:36.382 --> 00:06:38.172
If I see that you're cool.

00:06:38.172 --> 00:06:40.492
Like, you know, if we
could do a job together,

00:06:40.492 --> 00:06:41.481
like we'll do it.

00:06:41.481 --> 00:06:42.951
Most of the time, I do my jobs on my own

00:06:42.951 --> 00:06:46.427
because I don't like nobody
knowing what I'm doing.

00:06:46.427 --> 00:06:49.002
There's always snitches around, so.

00:06:49.002 --> 00:06:50.001
- [Interviewer] But no jail time?

00:06:50.001 --> 00:06:50.834
- Huh?

00:06:50.834 --> 00:06:51.667
- [Interviewer] No prison time?

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:52.642
- I've never actually been to prison,

00:06:52.642 --> 00:06:55.242
but I've been to jail
a whole lot of times.

00:06:55.242 --> 00:06:57.402
This last time, I was like going on three.

00:06:57.402 --> 00:07:00.152
I just got out like two and
a half, three years ago.

00:07:00.152 --> 00:07:03.485
I did 11 months for a whole gang of dope

00:07:04.987 --> 00:07:07.730
that I got caught up with it.

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:09.335
It wasn't mine.

00:07:09.335 --> 00:07:12.482
It was actually family member's

00:07:12.482 --> 00:07:17.192
and a guy that I was
messing with at that time.

00:07:17.192 --> 00:07:19.215
And I had my kids with me,

00:07:19.215 --> 00:07:21.072
but it was like, I had no record.

00:07:21.072 --> 00:07:24.321
And you know, my dude or whatever he was,

00:07:24.321 --> 00:07:25.748
who I was messing with at the time,

00:07:25.748 --> 00:07:28.698
like he would have went
to jail for a long time.

00:07:28.698 --> 00:07:31.021
My family member would
have did a lot of time

00:07:31.021 --> 00:07:31.937
and then got deported.

00:07:31.937 --> 00:07:34.331
So in order to kind of
save them and everything

00:07:34.331 --> 00:07:36.601
and not make it such a big deal,

00:07:36.601 --> 00:07:38.321
I took the fall for everything.

00:07:38.321 --> 00:07:40.404
And yeah, I went to jail.

00:07:41.391 --> 00:07:44.461
They got me for intent to distribute

00:07:44.461 --> 00:07:45.921
because I only had the dope.

00:07:45.921 --> 00:07:48.841
I didn't have a scale, no bags,
no money, no none of that,

00:07:48.841 --> 00:07:51.861
so they couldn't get me for sales,

00:07:51.861 --> 00:07:53.213
but they gave me two and a half

00:07:53.213 --> 00:07:55.961
and I ended up doing 11 months.

00:07:55.961 --> 00:07:57.391
But it's just,

00:07:57.391 --> 00:07:59.001
I think with the whole,

00:07:59.001 --> 00:08:01.621
that whole thing that went down,

00:08:01.621 --> 00:08:06.017
you know, that's when
detectives get involved

00:08:06.017 --> 00:08:08.105
and they try to sit you down.

00:08:08.105 --> 00:08:09.381
It's like a real life,

00:08:09.381 --> 00:08:10.422
like how you see it in the movies

00:08:10.422 --> 00:08:12.871
when they sit you at table and two chairs

00:08:12.871 --> 00:08:14.141
in an empty ass room.

00:08:14.141 --> 00:08:15.498
You know, he's like, sit down,

00:08:15.498 --> 00:08:17.175
and he's like, we can
make all this go away.

00:08:17.175 --> 00:08:19.421
And I was just like, no.

00:08:19.421 --> 00:08:20.761
I'm good, you know?

00:08:20.761 --> 00:08:22.002
Fuck you, like.

00:08:22.002 --> 00:08:23.372
He's like, you just got to do three jobs.

00:08:23.372 --> 00:08:24.205
I was like, I'm good.

00:08:24.205 --> 00:08:25.582
Look, I know what I did.

00:08:25.582 --> 00:08:26.415
I admitted it.

00:08:26.415 --> 00:08:28.226
Just give me my time, you know.

00:08:28.226 --> 00:08:31.491
And so the consequences of that

00:08:31.491 --> 00:08:33.573
was like me basically losing my kids.

00:08:33.573 --> 00:08:35.432
- [Interviewer] They wanted
you to be an informant?

00:08:35.432 --> 00:08:36.265
- Yeah.

00:08:36.265 --> 00:08:37.511
And I just, I couldn't do it.

00:08:37.511 --> 00:08:38.971
So I got bailed out.

00:08:38.971 --> 00:08:40.563
And when I went to court,

00:08:40.563 --> 00:08:42.591
I had that dude that I was
messing with at the time,

00:08:42.591 --> 00:08:43.755
he went with me.

00:08:43.755 --> 00:08:46.842
And even my attorney
or the public defender,

00:08:46.842 --> 00:08:48.249
he was like, you know,

00:08:48.249 --> 00:08:50.563
can I talk to you like
on the side or whatever?

00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:51.921
So we kind of moved to the side,

00:08:51.921 --> 00:08:53.817
but like, the dude was still
sitting there so he can hear.

00:08:53.817 --> 00:08:55.762
And he's like, okay, so
you're helping the detective.

00:08:55.762 --> 00:08:57.470
And I was like, no, the fuck I'm not.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.062
'Cause it could be any
little thing they say

00:08:59.062 --> 00:09:00.902
and it's like, anybody hears it.

00:09:00.902 --> 00:09:01.985
Like, that's it.

00:09:01.985 --> 00:09:03.071
You're burnt, you're done.

00:09:03.071 --> 00:09:03.904
You know?

00:09:03.904 --> 00:09:04.737
And I was like, nah, fuck that.

00:09:04.737 --> 00:09:05.570
Take that off my record.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:06.822
I'm not helping no fucking detective,

00:09:06.822 --> 00:09:07.655
none of that shit.

00:09:07.655 --> 00:09:09.355
Like, just give me my time.

00:09:09.355 --> 00:09:11.272
'Cause he's like, well, I can't help you.

00:09:11.272 --> 00:09:12.105
You know?

00:09:12.105 --> 00:09:12.938
I was like, I don't care.

00:09:12.938 --> 00:09:13.771
I'm not asking you to help me.

00:09:13.771 --> 00:09:15.952
Just give me my time and that's it.

00:09:15.952 --> 00:09:16.785
You know?

00:09:16.785 --> 00:09:19.179
I didn't ask for your help.

00:09:19.179 --> 00:09:20.458
Just tell the judge
whatever needs to be said

00:09:20.458 --> 00:09:21.291
and that's it.

00:09:21.291 --> 00:09:24.172
Give my time and I'll be out of your way.

00:09:24.172 --> 00:09:25.863
And he was like, all right.

00:09:25.863 --> 00:09:28.124
And I think that's the
first time I ever got scared

00:09:28.124 --> 00:09:32.432
as far as like dealing with
the whole gang environment

00:09:32.432 --> 00:09:35.693
because people don't play when
it comes to shit like that.

00:09:35.693 --> 00:09:37.647
And I'm definitely not no informant.

00:09:37.647 --> 00:09:40.243
And, I mean, as far as the way I grew up

00:09:40.243 --> 00:09:42.636
and the people I grew up around,

00:09:42.636 --> 00:09:45.536
that's just something you don't do.

00:09:45.536 --> 00:09:47.141
I know the game has been
washed up a little bit,

00:09:47.141 --> 00:09:49.141
but you know, my values,

00:09:50.188 --> 00:09:54.105
all the rules I go by
are from back in the day.

00:09:55.526 --> 00:09:57.193
It's just, you know?

00:09:58.057 --> 00:10:02.422
That's kind of why I'm still
doing the same shit like now.

00:10:02.422 --> 00:10:04.162
Tomorrow, I'll be 33.

00:10:04.162 --> 00:10:06.483
And I was in a program.

00:10:06.483 --> 00:10:10.672
I literally snuck out last
night to go see my dude.

00:10:10.672 --> 00:10:12.843
And that went all bad.

00:10:12.843 --> 00:10:14.904
And then I'm back here at skid row,

00:10:14.904 --> 00:10:17.042
fucking same shit, back
and forth, back and forth,

00:10:17.042 --> 00:10:20.230
because it's like you want to do good,

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:22.647
but you know, all the damage,

00:10:23.487 --> 00:10:25.282
all the chaos you've caused in your past,

00:10:25.282 --> 00:10:27.293
it's like there's barriers.

00:10:27.293 --> 00:10:29.233
There's obstacles you've gotta go through

00:10:29.233 --> 00:10:31.712
and it's not always easy for a female.

00:10:31.712 --> 00:10:35.307
And so, yeah, like I just, you know.

00:10:35.307 --> 00:10:37.138
- [Interviewer] Did you raise any kids?

00:10:37.138 --> 00:10:40.203
- I raised them for the first few years.

00:10:40.203 --> 00:10:42.402
My youngest one is probably the only one

00:10:42.402 --> 00:10:44.804
that I didn't really raise.

00:10:44.804 --> 00:10:48.167
She was a year when they took her from me.

00:10:48.167 --> 00:10:52.439
And it was so stupid too
because I had been clean.

00:10:52.439 --> 00:10:54.585
I was clean and the social worker came

00:10:54.585 --> 00:10:55.872
and they had been trying
to get ahold of me.

00:10:55.872 --> 00:10:57.715
They were living with
their dad at the time

00:10:57.715 --> 00:10:59.636
and I was just kind of everywhere.

00:10:59.636 --> 00:11:00.793
And they were like, you know,

00:11:00.793 --> 00:11:02.847
we need you to come in and test.

00:11:02.847 --> 00:11:05.503
And I had been clean for like
at least three, four days.

00:11:05.503 --> 00:11:08.722
And the day of the test,
I went and got high.

00:11:08.722 --> 00:11:11.193
And it was like, who the fuck
thinks of shit like that?

00:11:11.193 --> 00:11:13.501
Like your whole case
could have been closed

00:11:13.501 --> 00:11:14.997
if you would've just waited to go test

00:11:14.997 --> 00:11:18.579
and then go get high or
not get high, you know?

00:11:18.579 --> 00:11:21.777
But that's just how
fucking addict minds think,

00:11:21.777 --> 00:11:22.994
or we don't think.

00:11:22.994 --> 00:11:24.459
We just do.

00:11:24.459 --> 00:11:25.292
- [Interviewer] Do you think

00:11:25.292 --> 00:11:26.362
there's some self-destructive streak

00:11:26.362 --> 00:11:28.222
that just makes you kind
of sabotage yourself?

00:11:28.222 --> 00:11:29.731
- Yeah, all the time.

00:11:29.731 --> 00:11:33.562
We were talking about this
in rehab the other day,

00:11:33.562 --> 00:11:35.891
like, you know, just self-destruction,

00:11:35.891 --> 00:11:36.832
self-sabotage,

00:11:36.832 --> 00:11:40.457
fear of not knowing if I can succeed

00:11:40.457 --> 00:11:42.291
or if I can make shit happen.

00:11:42.291 --> 00:11:43.133
Like, yeah.

00:11:43.133 --> 00:11:45.155
So it makes you just not want to do it.

00:11:45.155 --> 00:11:46.411
It makes you not want to try it.

00:11:46.411 --> 00:11:48.332
And it's easier to just fuck everything up

00:11:48.332 --> 00:11:51.332
'cause I know my kids are good,

00:11:51.332 --> 00:11:52.861
like well taken care of.

00:11:52.861 --> 00:11:54.111
They're in the system,

00:11:54.111 --> 00:11:55.061
but they're not in the system.

00:11:55.061 --> 00:11:56.822
You know, they've always been with family.

00:11:56.822 --> 00:11:59.889
So I think I use that like
to just be like, fuck it.

00:11:59.889 --> 00:12:02.133
Like, I can't give them nothing right now.

00:12:02.133 --> 00:12:03.498
Like, I can't give them a home.

00:12:03.498 --> 00:12:04.671
I can't feed them.

00:12:04.671 --> 00:12:05.754
I can't do shit,

00:12:05.754 --> 00:12:08.303
so I just kind of go with that.

00:12:08.303 --> 00:12:09.502
And I know I shouldn't,

00:12:09.502 --> 00:12:12.307
but that goes along with just guilt

00:12:12.307 --> 00:12:14.441
and the shit I've put them through,

00:12:14.441 --> 00:12:15.916
the shit they've seen.

00:12:15.916 --> 00:12:19.862
And it's no shit that kids
should never see, you know?

00:12:19.862 --> 00:12:22.219
Like sitting here taking a gang of pills

00:12:22.219 --> 00:12:23.213
trying to kill myself,

00:12:23.213 --> 00:12:24.165
and the kids are looking at me

00:12:24.165 --> 00:12:25.452
like what's going on with mom?

00:12:25.452 --> 00:12:28.587
And rushing me out the
house to the hospital.

00:12:28.587 --> 00:12:32.147
And it's like kids don't
need to see like that.

00:12:32.147 --> 00:12:34.565
It was just so much
violence, so much violence.

00:12:34.565 --> 00:12:36.412
My kids seen a lot of violence.

00:12:36.412 --> 00:12:39.633
And I'm talking about
not just going heads up.

00:12:39.633 --> 00:12:41.292
I mean, like destroying the whole house,

00:12:41.292 --> 00:12:44.087
you know, barricading
yourself in the house,

00:12:44.087 --> 00:12:46.792
throwing knives,
stabbing, like everything.

00:12:46.792 --> 00:12:48.931
Had them living in room to room.

00:12:48.931 --> 00:12:53.848
Like, it's like shit that kids
don't need to see, you know?

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:59.763
So right now, I feel like
I'm living out my karma type,

00:13:00.705 --> 00:13:01.538
you know?

00:13:03.636 --> 00:13:04.469
Who knows?

00:13:04.469 --> 00:13:07.131
Maybe God has something
different for me later on,

00:13:07.131 --> 00:13:08.394
but for right now.

00:13:08.394 --> 00:13:10.531
I mean, I've even lied to my parents.

00:13:10.531 --> 00:13:12.056
I was like, I'm not gonna leave.

00:13:12.056 --> 00:13:13.922
This is the last time.

00:13:13.922 --> 00:13:16.812
I've never had a
breakthrough with my mother.

00:13:16.812 --> 00:13:20.131
And when I was at the
rehab a couple of days ago,

00:13:20.131 --> 00:13:22.010
like I finally text her.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:23.262
And in all honesty,

00:13:23.262 --> 00:13:24.267
I only text her 'cause I knew

00:13:24.267 --> 00:13:25.451
she was gonna bring me money,

00:13:25.451 --> 00:13:26.861
and cigarettes, and stuff like that.

00:13:26.861 --> 00:13:29.162
So I was like, let me
just hit her up real quick

00:13:29.162 --> 00:13:30.311
and so I did.

00:13:30.311 --> 00:13:31.862
But it was like a whole 'nother experience

00:13:31.862 --> 00:13:34.092
because as soon as I hit her up,

00:13:34.092 --> 00:13:35.111
you know, it was just a quick text.

00:13:35.111 --> 00:13:36.271
She was at work.

00:13:36.271 --> 00:13:40.096
And she was like, asking if I was okay,

00:13:40.096 --> 00:13:41.521
why haven't I hit her up or whatever.

00:13:41.521 --> 00:13:42.564
And then she was like,

00:13:42.564 --> 00:13:44.151
when I get off of work,
I'm gonna call you.

00:13:44.151 --> 00:13:45.309
And I'm over here,

00:13:45.309 --> 00:13:46.142
like well don't call me

00:13:46.142 --> 00:13:48.163
because I'm not supposed
to have a phone in rehab,

00:13:48.163 --> 00:13:49.041
but I do.

00:13:49.041 --> 00:13:50.651
So just text me and I'll call you.

00:13:50.651 --> 00:13:53.264
So she calls me and she's crying.

00:13:53.264 --> 00:13:55.611
And for me, for my mother to cry

00:13:55.611 --> 00:13:58.002
because of the shit I'm doing

00:13:58.002 --> 00:14:01.159
is something I've never like experienced.

00:14:01.159 --> 00:14:02.523
We never had that bond, you know?

00:14:02.523 --> 00:14:04.046
So she's like, you know what?

00:14:04.046 --> 00:14:05.170
You know you are my daughter.

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:06.003
You think I don't love you?

00:14:06.003 --> 00:14:07.716
You don't think I don't worry?

00:14:07.716 --> 00:14:09.922
And like, that shit made me cry

00:14:09.922 --> 00:14:12.168
only 'cause we've never had that.

00:14:12.168 --> 00:14:13.008
So I'm just like, damn.

00:14:13.008 --> 00:14:14.858
Like, I really am a fucked up ass.

00:14:14.858 --> 00:14:16.958
Like, she pays for my phone.

00:14:16.958 --> 00:14:17.889
Like, she's been paying for my phone

00:14:17.889 --> 00:14:18.843
since I got out of jail.

00:14:18.843 --> 00:14:19.943
It's going on three years.

00:14:19.943 --> 00:14:22.124
I don't give her shit for the phone

00:14:22.124 --> 00:14:23.094
and I got a brand new phone.

00:14:23.094 --> 00:14:24.973
Like, I don't pay the bill every month

00:14:24.973 --> 00:14:26.678
and she just keeps paying.

00:14:26.678 --> 00:14:28.678
Sure enough, she was like,

00:14:28.678 --> 00:14:29.723
I'm gonna take you cigarettes,

00:14:29.723 --> 00:14:30.769
I'm gonna take you money,

00:14:30.769 --> 00:14:31.978
I'm gonna take you food.

00:14:31.978 --> 00:14:34.730
And I was like, I'm not
gonna leave this time.

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:35.563
It's different.

00:14:35.563 --> 00:14:36.739
Like, you know?

00:14:36.739 --> 00:14:40.448
And here the fuck I am
again back on Skid Row

00:14:40.448 --> 00:14:43.589
and she don't even know it yet,

00:14:43.589 --> 00:14:45.672
but I mean, I don't know.

00:14:47.742 --> 00:14:50.552
Being an addict is fucked up.

00:14:50.552 --> 00:14:53.056
Like we don't ever think
about the consequences

00:14:53.056 --> 00:14:56.083
or the people we hurt when
we're in our addiction,

00:14:56.083 --> 00:14:56.919
you know?

00:14:56.919 --> 00:14:58.263
- [Interviewer] Have you
been through rehab a lot?

00:14:58.263 --> 00:14:59.096
- Yes.

00:14:59.096 --> 00:15:00.373
It's like at least my ninth,

00:15:00.373 --> 00:15:01.873
10th time being in rehab.

00:15:01.873 --> 00:15:04.153
I've completed only two times.

00:15:04.153 --> 00:15:07.039
The rest is just either
I'm about to complete it

00:15:07.039 --> 00:15:08.065
and I fuck up,

00:15:08.065 --> 00:15:11.229
or I'm just like, you know what, I'm out.

00:15:11.229 --> 00:15:12.999
Which that's mostly what it is.

00:15:12.999 --> 00:15:14.659
It's like I get there and
stay there a day or two.

00:15:14.659 --> 00:15:17.124
And it's like, all right, I'm gone.

00:15:17.124 --> 00:15:17.957
This last time,

00:15:17.957 --> 00:15:19.872
I probably went back
like six times already

00:15:19.872 --> 00:15:21.628
in the last month.

00:15:21.628 --> 00:15:22.552
And that's only 'cause

00:15:22.552 --> 00:15:24.750
I'm tired of being here on the streets.

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:27.609
And I think this last run
was probably the first time

00:15:27.609 --> 00:15:30.809
I've ever actually been on Skid Row,

00:15:30.809 --> 00:15:32.476
like actually in it.

00:15:33.537 --> 00:15:36.701
And it's just, it's a crazy experience.

00:15:36.701 --> 00:15:38.494
But you know,

00:15:38.494 --> 00:15:41.530
my mom always says if I could
just slap you out of it,

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:42.363
you'll be good.

00:15:42.363 --> 00:15:43.196
And I'm just like,

00:15:43.196 --> 00:15:45.330
well, if you can slap
the addiction out of us,

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:46.979
then nobody would be addicts.

00:15:46.979 --> 00:15:48.369
Like, you know, we
wouldn't have this problem,

00:15:48.369 --> 00:15:50.559
but you know, here we are.

00:15:50.559 --> 00:15:52.744
So, I mean, I don't know.

00:15:52.744 --> 00:15:55.319
I didn't really go into much details, but.

00:15:55.319 --> 00:15:56.152
- [Interviewer] Do you think

00:15:56.152 --> 00:15:57.199
that the problem is the addiction

00:15:57.199 --> 00:16:00.532
or do you think it's the low self-worth,

00:16:01.415 --> 00:16:02.464
what you believe,

00:16:02.464 --> 00:16:04.693
you believe you deserve crap so you?

00:16:04.693 --> 00:16:07.324
- I think it's more of the lifestyle

00:16:07.324 --> 00:16:09.635
because I mean, I just
had a breakthrough too

00:16:09.635 --> 00:16:13.144
with the whole like guilt and
and feeling like, you know,

00:16:13.144 --> 00:16:16.012
the fear of the unknown for the future.

00:16:16.012 --> 00:16:19.617
You know, if I get my kids
back, will I lose them again?

00:16:19.617 --> 00:16:21.528
But I think it's more
of like the lifestyle

00:16:21.528 --> 00:16:24.334
because I mean, there's
times where I have done good.

00:16:24.334 --> 00:16:26.068
I was with a guy.

00:16:26.068 --> 00:16:27.045
We moved to Tracy.

00:16:27.045 --> 00:16:28.818
We had a five-bedroom house, cars.

00:16:28.818 --> 00:16:32.799
The kids went to like the
best white school, you know?

00:16:32.799 --> 00:16:34.072
Schools where you gotta, like,

00:16:34.072 --> 00:16:36.548
it's not an option for you
to donate to the school.

00:16:36.548 --> 00:16:38.958
It's an obligation, you know?

00:16:38.958 --> 00:16:42.509
And I've had a good life, you know?

00:16:42.509 --> 00:16:43.342
Here and there.

00:16:43.342 --> 00:16:45.703
But there's times where I was, I was good.

00:16:45.703 --> 00:16:48.069
And it's still, it's still the lifestyle.

00:16:48.069 --> 00:16:49.839
The lifestyle is like, you know,

00:16:49.839 --> 00:16:52.300
I'm in an area where I don't know nobody.

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:54.854
And I always feel like
I gotta defend myself,

00:16:54.854 --> 00:16:57.650
so if somebody comes at me talking proper

00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:59.928
or saying some stuff that
I don't really understand,

00:16:59.928 --> 00:17:02.800
like I'll take it as
like they're attacking.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:03.633
And it's not.

00:17:03.633 --> 00:17:05.608
It's just 'cause like I'm
so close minded sometimes

00:17:05.608 --> 00:17:09.350
that I don't try to
understand the next person.

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:11.775
And I'm just so quick to, you know,

00:17:11.775 --> 00:17:12.776
like fuck it.

00:17:12.776 --> 00:17:15.173
Like, all right, so what's next?

00:17:15.173 --> 00:17:16.450
You know, like move on.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:19.311
And I'm really good at leaving, you know?

00:17:19.311 --> 00:17:21.170
Like if something don't go right

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:23.261
or if I fuck it up enough,

00:17:23.261 --> 00:17:24.221
I'm gone, you know?

00:17:24.221 --> 00:17:26.711
And I'll disappear for
like couple of days,

00:17:26.711 --> 00:17:28.612
couple of weeks, couple years,

00:17:28.612 --> 00:17:31.200
come back and start the
process all over again.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:32.354
Start doing good,

00:17:32.354 --> 00:17:34.061
then realize, all right, I'm doing good.

00:17:34.061 --> 00:17:35.461
Like, you know, I can get high real quick

00:17:35.461 --> 00:17:37.780
or I could go make this
quick money or whatever.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:40.052
And then that's when it starts all over

00:17:40.052 --> 00:17:42.060
and just start losing
shit little by little

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:44.260
until I'm back here.

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:45.932
And that's just kind of how it's been

00:17:45.932 --> 00:17:48.432
for the past 12, 13, 14 years.

00:17:50.203 --> 00:17:53.703
And I wish I could say like, this is done,

00:17:56.890 --> 00:18:00.322
but I don't know because I know inside,

00:18:00.322 --> 00:18:01.155
I do want to feel,

00:18:01.155 --> 00:18:02.840
like I do feel like this is over now

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:03.855
and I want to turn my life around,

00:18:03.855 --> 00:18:05.778
but then it's like any
little thing will happen.

00:18:05.778 --> 00:18:07.677
Like for instance, you know, this morning,

00:18:07.677 --> 00:18:09.917
like I'm over here chilling
with this dude or whatever.

00:18:09.917 --> 00:18:12.176
And because he's coming
down off of his shit,

00:18:12.176 --> 00:18:13.127
we kind of get into it.

00:18:13.127 --> 00:18:14.707
And then now it's like, well, fuck it,

00:18:14.707 --> 00:18:15.707
I'm not going back to the program.

00:18:15.707 --> 00:18:16.877
And I still have a chance to go back

00:18:16.877 --> 00:18:17.967
without them knowing I left.

00:18:17.967 --> 00:18:21.304
But it's like, look
where I end up, you know?

00:18:21.304 --> 00:18:23.227
End up here fucking getting high.

00:18:23.227 --> 00:18:25.652
And it's just, it's crazy, it's crazy.

00:18:25.652 --> 00:18:27.569
This addiction is real.

00:18:28.737 --> 00:18:29.904
It's powerful.

00:18:31.457 --> 00:18:32.290
- [Interviewer] What do you think

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.737
most people don't
understand about addiction

00:18:34.737 --> 00:18:36.487
that are not addicts?

00:18:36.487 --> 00:18:40.538
- I think the biggest
thing they struggle with

00:18:40.538 --> 00:18:42.581
is just not understanding,

00:18:42.581 --> 00:18:45.687
like not understanding
what the drug does to you

00:18:45.687 --> 00:18:47.637
as far as your body, your mind,

00:18:47.637 --> 00:18:49.912
as far as the whole craving,

00:18:49.912 --> 00:18:52.087
like releasing dopamine, all of that.

00:18:52.087 --> 00:18:54.317
They get into all of the
details when you're in rehab,

00:18:54.317 --> 00:18:57.434
but it's like when you're not an addict,

00:18:57.434 --> 00:19:02.434
or even for the addicts who
like are functional addicts

00:19:02.466 --> 00:19:05.788
or like occasional addicts, you know,

00:19:05.788 --> 00:19:08.778
even they don't understand.

00:19:08.778 --> 00:19:12.637
It's kinda like having a sugar craving,

00:19:12.637 --> 00:19:14.795
a chocolate craving or
whatever, or a hobby.

00:19:14.795 --> 00:19:16.415
Like, it's like if you like biking,

00:19:16.415 --> 00:19:17.745
it's like you don't know why you do it.

00:19:17.745 --> 00:19:18.715
I mean, well, you know why you do it,

00:19:18.715 --> 00:19:20.900
but whatever feeling it gives you,

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:22.755
that's what makes you
want to keep doing it.

00:19:22.755 --> 00:19:23.588
You know?

00:19:23.588 --> 00:19:26.675
People that hike, people that golf.

00:19:26.675 --> 00:19:28.750
It just makes you feel a certain way

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:32.080
and that is exactly what dope does.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:33.435
- [Interviewer] It becomes
your first priority.

00:19:33.435 --> 00:19:34.393
- Right.

00:19:34.393 --> 00:19:37.216
It's not even like second nature.

00:19:37.216 --> 00:19:39.060
It's like just first
nature type shit, you know?

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:40.064
- [Interviewer] It seems
like more than survival.

00:19:40.064 --> 00:19:40.904
- Right.

00:19:40.904 --> 00:19:41.979
And then you got the drugs

00:19:41.979 --> 00:19:45.044
that make you actually physically sick

00:19:45.044 --> 00:19:47.042
if you don't keep using, you know?

00:19:47.042 --> 00:19:49.375
The type where your whole
body could shut down.

00:19:49.375 --> 00:19:50.595
Luckily, meth is not like that.

00:19:50.595 --> 00:19:52.914
It's just, you sleep for a couple of days

00:19:52.914 --> 00:19:54.766
and you wake up and you're good.

00:19:54.766 --> 00:19:56.194
You might feel a little weak

00:19:56.194 --> 00:19:57.444
'cause you're overworking your body,

00:19:57.444 --> 00:19:59.769
but there's no actual physical pain

00:19:59.769 --> 00:20:03.800
where you need to like
be medicated or whatnot.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:07.095
So that's why I always feel
like I don't have it that bad,

00:20:07.095 --> 00:20:09.693
but I mean, any drug that you do is bad.

00:20:09.693 --> 00:20:11.190
It doesn't matter how
bad it makes you feel

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:12.859
when you're coming off of it or not.

00:20:12.859 --> 00:20:13.864
It's about where it takes you

00:20:13.864 --> 00:20:16.034
while you're in your addiction, you know?

00:20:16.034 --> 00:20:19.394
And it's just, people do crazy shit.

00:20:19.394 --> 00:20:22.660
You'd be surprised like the shit,

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:23.493
this whole past year,

00:20:23.493 --> 00:20:24.434
the shit I've been going through,

00:20:24.434 --> 00:20:26.194
the shit I put up with
just because the dope.

00:20:26.194 --> 00:20:29.149
Like all the fighting,
all the getting beat up.

00:20:29.149 --> 00:20:31.124
Like, it's just, it's crazy,

00:20:31.124 --> 00:20:33.904
but for whatever reason, we deal with it.

00:20:33.904 --> 00:20:34.987
We accept it.

00:20:34.987 --> 00:20:35.820
We live it.

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:39.733
We give that same negative
energy to the next person

00:20:39.733 --> 00:20:42.844
and it's all because we
just want to be high.

00:20:42.844 --> 00:20:47.043
- [Interviewer] Do you feel
like it's a generational curse?

00:20:47.043 --> 00:20:49.874
- It's maybe not a curse.

00:20:49.874 --> 00:20:51.440
It's more of like,

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:53.203
I mean, I guess you
could see it as a curse.

00:20:53.203 --> 00:20:54.654
- [Interviewer] I see it as role models.

00:20:54.654 --> 00:20:55.487
The role models you had--

00:20:55.487 --> 00:20:56.320
- Well, yeah,

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:59.783
because when we were growing up,

00:20:59.783 --> 00:21:02.415
my stepdad, he used a lot.

00:21:02.415 --> 00:21:04.522
I mean, he was high every day,

00:21:04.522 --> 00:21:07.043
but he always went to work.

00:21:07.043 --> 00:21:08.696
We never were homeless.

00:21:08.696 --> 00:21:10.153
We never were out of food.

00:21:10.153 --> 00:21:11.512
Like, we always had everything,

00:21:11.512 --> 00:21:13.043
but he was always high.

00:21:13.043 --> 00:21:14.563
And yeah, he did the whole,

00:21:14.563 --> 00:21:17.433
my mom had people living behind the TV

00:21:17.433 --> 00:21:19.563
and there was all kinds
of guys everywhere.

00:21:19.563 --> 00:21:20.824
And I know that was in his mind,

00:21:20.824 --> 00:21:23.384
but when you're small,
you don't know that.

00:21:23.384 --> 00:21:25.993
So then when I started using,

00:21:25.993 --> 00:21:28.632
I was using with my baby's dad.

00:21:28.632 --> 00:21:29.465
I know for a while,

00:21:29.465 --> 00:21:32.083
he thought that it was his
fault why I started using,

00:21:32.083 --> 00:21:34.384
but I told him, you know, after a while,

00:21:34.384 --> 00:21:37.354
it's like you can't force
somebody to get high, you know?

00:21:37.354 --> 00:21:40.225
Even if you did encourage it to try it,

00:21:40.225 --> 00:21:42.752
it was my choice after
that to keep on using.

00:21:42.752 --> 00:21:46.323
And it ended up being a
drug that I loved, you know?

00:21:46.323 --> 00:21:48.344
So I've used every day.

00:21:48.344 --> 00:21:52.523
And yeah, it got to a point
where I was using with my dad.

00:21:52.523 --> 00:21:55.918
Up until the day I got
arrested this last time,

00:21:55.918 --> 00:21:58.426
I was with my dad all the time,

00:21:58.426 --> 00:21:59.838
always going to work with him,

00:21:59.838 --> 00:22:00.815
you know, everything.

00:22:00.815 --> 00:22:02.262
It got to a point

00:22:02.262 --> 00:22:05.595
where my dad was kind of having problems

00:22:07.094 --> 00:22:08.800
with one of my brothers

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:11.636
and his wife decided to call the cops

00:22:11.636 --> 00:22:13.396
and kind of say everything.

00:22:13.396 --> 00:22:14.840
And she's like, yeah,

00:22:14.840 --> 00:22:17.800
well, you know, she's over here.

00:22:17.800 --> 00:22:19.674
Like her and her dad
over here are fucking.

00:22:19.674 --> 00:22:21.087
And I was like, what the fuck?

00:22:21.087 --> 00:22:22.173
Like, bitch.

00:22:22.173 --> 00:22:24.171
I had my sisters calling
me, like what the fuck,

00:22:24.171 --> 00:22:25.256
talking shit.

00:22:25.256 --> 00:22:26.754
And I was like, what the fuck
are you guys talking about?

00:22:26.754 --> 00:22:28.508
My mom's calling me, talking shit.

00:22:28.508 --> 00:22:29.842
And I was just like,

00:22:29.842 --> 00:22:32.509
what in your right fucking
mind makes you think

00:22:32.509 --> 00:22:33.799
that I would ever sleep with my dad?

00:22:33.799 --> 00:22:34.921
Like I know he's not my real dad,

00:22:34.921 --> 00:22:36.341
but he's my dad to me.

00:22:36.341 --> 00:22:38.591
I was a little ass girl
when he came into our life,

00:22:38.591 --> 00:22:40.419
so to me, that's my dad.

00:22:40.419 --> 00:22:42.551
And it was a big issue

00:22:42.551 --> 00:22:45.461
because my mom and him
weren't living together.

00:22:45.461 --> 00:22:46.760
At the time, she was living in Arizona.

00:22:46.760 --> 00:22:48.551
He was living with my brother.

00:22:48.551 --> 00:22:50.252
He kind of had the back room.

00:22:50.252 --> 00:22:51.341
It was like all the way in the back.

00:22:51.341 --> 00:22:54.217
And it was just like, yeah,
I was always with my dad.

00:22:54.217 --> 00:22:56.173
Yeah, I could sleep in
the same room as my dad,

00:22:56.173 --> 00:22:58.554
but he'll either be on the
bed or on the floor, you know?

00:22:58.554 --> 00:23:01.131
Like it was never that type of shit.

00:23:01.131 --> 00:23:02.611
And it caused a lot of drama.

00:23:02.611 --> 00:23:04.740
Of course, it plants that seed
in people's minds, you know?

00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:07.305
Like, okay, well, they're
both not saying it,

00:23:07.305 --> 00:23:08.138
but who knows?

00:23:08.138 --> 00:23:08.971
It could have happened.

00:23:08.971 --> 00:23:09.929
They're both getting high.

00:23:09.929 --> 00:23:11.693
People do shit when they're high.

00:23:11.693 --> 00:23:14.276
And it was just like, you know.

00:23:16.746 --> 00:23:19.503
Yeah, that put a big,
big wall in between me

00:23:19.503 --> 00:23:22.086
and a lot of my family members.

00:23:23.725 --> 00:23:25.992
And I mean, I ain't got
nothing to lie about.

00:23:25.992 --> 00:23:28.848
I know in my heart that
has never happened.

00:23:28.848 --> 00:23:31.218
It would never happen.

00:23:31.218 --> 00:23:35.348
But yeah, when I went to
jail, my dad got sick.

00:23:35.348 --> 00:23:36.982
You know, he was dying.

00:23:36.982 --> 00:23:38.933
His heart gave up.

00:23:38.933 --> 00:23:42.067
That's when he decided to
change his life around.

00:23:42.067 --> 00:23:43.572
And I didn't know nothing about it

00:23:43.572 --> 00:23:45.512
until I actually got out of jail.

00:23:45.512 --> 00:23:47.417
And he was on all these medications.

00:23:47.417 --> 00:23:50.062
He had lost so much weight.

00:23:50.062 --> 00:23:52.272
It was kind of an eye opener.

00:23:52.272 --> 00:23:55.333
and I was happy to see
that my dad was clean,

00:23:55.333 --> 00:23:59.323
but for whatever reason,
it wasn't enough for me.

00:23:59.323 --> 00:24:01.990
you know, it wasn't my time yet.

00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:04.690
And I would say like,

00:24:06.292 --> 00:24:07.782
just because it's around you

00:24:07.782 --> 00:24:09.429
or just because you grew up that way,

00:24:09.429 --> 00:24:10.532
it doesn't always mean

00:24:10.532 --> 00:24:14.103
that you need to follow those same steps.

00:24:14.103 --> 00:24:16.842
Everybody still knows
right from wrong, you know?

00:24:16.842 --> 00:24:18.803
Even if your whole household does dope

00:24:18.803 --> 00:24:21.102
or are gang bangers or whatever,

00:24:21.102 --> 00:24:24.263
it's like you get to a certain
age where you know yourself.

00:24:24.263 --> 00:24:26.222
Do you want to join this?

00:24:26.222 --> 00:24:27.172
Do you want to be a part of it

00:24:27.172 --> 00:24:28.812
or do you want to live a different life?

00:24:28.812 --> 00:24:29.645
You know?

00:24:29.645 --> 00:24:31.674
So I never really blamed like my addiction

00:24:31.674 --> 00:24:36.152
or anything that I do on like
from growing up, you know,

00:24:36.152 --> 00:24:39.584
because I mean, I don't really
care how stupid you are,

00:24:39.584 --> 00:24:42.311
you always know right from wrong.

00:24:42.311 --> 00:24:44.812
And of course, I like the adrenaline.

00:24:44.812 --> 00:24:46.145
I like the rush.

00:24:46.145 --> 00:24:47.485
I like taking risks.

00:24:47.485 --> 00:24:49.749
I like doing that I know
I could get caught up for.

00:24:49.749 --> 00:24:53.558
And so that's why I
just kinda went with it.

00:24:53.558 --> 00:24:55.672
But then, yeah, I have
a problem with authority

00:24:55.672 --> 00:24:57.652
so I've just kind of never
did the whole gang thing.

00:24:57.652 --> 00:25:01.152
I used to hang around with
them and do certain jobs,

00:25:01.152 --> 00:25:03.972
but I never actually became a gang member.

00:25:03.972 --> 00:25:06.022
And mainly because I was
just all over the place,

00:25:06.022 --> 00:25:07.872
different cities, different hoods.

00:25:07.872 --> 00:25:08.903
So it's like,

00:25:08.903 --> 00:25:10.869
I can't go to another place

00:25:10.869 --> 00:25:12.772
and be like, well, I can't talk
to you 'cause I'm from here.

00:25:12.772 --> 00:25:14.994
To me, I don't know
how that, I don't know.

00:25:14.994 --> 00:25:17.477
So I never really joined a gang, but yeah.

00:25:17.477 --> 00:25:19.521
I mean, I've been around
dope my whole life.

00:25:19.521 --> 00:25:20.882
You know, dope, alcohol.

00:25:20.882 --> 00:25:23.152
As far as for Mexicans in my family,

00:25:23.152 --> 00:25:26.848
you're never really an alcoholic
because everybody drinks.

00:25:26.848 --> 00:25:27.824
I think the only person

00:25:27.824 --> 00:25:29.963
who's actually ever considered
an alcoholic in my family

00:25:29.963 --> 00:25:31.177
was my grandpa.

00:25:31.177 --> 00:25:32.632
And that's 'cause he died from it

00:25:32.632 --> 00:25:34.127
when I was a little girl,

00:25:34.127 --> 00:25:38.213
who also, which I lied to
my mother about this too,

00:25:38.213 --> 00:25:41.512
kind of had a breakthrough
when I first got out of jail.

00:25:41.512 --> 00:25:42.345
It was Christmas.

00:25:42.345 --> 00:25:44.425
And it was just me and
like three of my sisters.

00:25:44.425 --> 00:25:47.262
And you know, I guess they were drunk

00:25:47.262 --> 00:25:48.485
and they were feeling some type of way,

00:25:48.485 --> 00:25:49.939
so feelings started coming out,

00:25:49.939 --> 00:25:52.717
and you did this when I was
small, and you did this.

00:25:52.717 --> 00:25:54.382
And my mom was like,

00:25:54.382 --> 00:25:56.592
well, my whole fear was that

00:25:56.592 --> 00:25:59.303
grandpa was gonna do something to you guys

00:25:59.303 --> 00:26:00.683
'cause he was a drunk.

00:26:00.683 --> 00:26:02.173
Like he didn't know what he was doing.

00:26:02.173 --> 00:26:03.366
And I looked at her

00:26:03.366 --> 00:26:06.382
and I didn't have the
heart to tell her like,

00:26:06.382 --> 00:26:09.105
well, yeah, it did happen.

00:26:09.105 --> 00:26:10.694
But I mean, if you were so scared

00:26:10.694 --> 00:26:12.251
that he was gonna do something to us,

00:26:12.251 --> 00:26:13.782
why did you put us in that situation?

00:26:13.782 --> 00:26:14.782
You know what I'm saying?

00:26:14.782 --> 00:26:16.624
Why did you have him there?

00:26:16.624 --> 00:26:17.902
So that's what I didn't
understand about it

00:26:17.902 --> 00:26:19.679
and that's why I didn't
tell her like, yeah,

00:26:19.679 --> 00:26:22.346
you know, like he did, he tried.

00:26:23.319 --> 00:26:25.223
But to me, that was my grandpa.

00:26:25.223 --> 00:26:28.424
And even though I didn't
let him do anything,

00:26:28.424 --> 00:26:31.082
I still couldn't be mad at him.

00:26:31.082 --> 00:26:34.533
You know, I couldn't hold
a grudge against him.

00:26:34.533 --> 00:26:36.967
I didn't have no resentments.

00:26:36.967 --> 00:26:37.800
I loved him.

00:26:37.800 --> 00:26:39.424
He was grandpa, you know?

00:26:39.424 --> 00:26:40.811
It didn't matter what day it was.

00:26:40.811 --> 00:26:41.913
He'll take you to the store,

00:26:41.913 --> 00:26:43.383
and he'll get his beer and his scratchers,

00:26:43.383 --> 00:26:44.678
and he'll let you scratch one.

00:26:44.678 --> 00:26:46.404
And that was our day with him, you know?

00:26:46.404 --> 00:26:48.097
And it was an everyday thing.

00:26:48.097 --> 00:26:49.157
But 'til this day,

00:26:49.157 --> 00:26:52.578
my mother does not know that he also tried

00:26:52.578 --> 00:26:54.912
and it was around the same time

00:26:54.912 --> 00:26:58.912
when their friend had did
what he had did to me.

00:27:01.767 --> 00:27:05.926
And I don't know if she'll ever see this,

00:27:05.926 --> 00:27:08.074
but I don't think I would ever
have the heart to tell her

00:27:08.074 --> 00:27:12.001
because I know that that was
one thing that she feared.

00:27:12.001 --> 00:27:14.934
She really broke down
and cried and told us,

00:27:14.934 --> 00:27:17.552
like, that was my only fear with you guys.

00:27:17.552 --> 00:27:20.154
And I mean, I kind of didn't want to

00:27:20.154 --> 00:27:21.616
like throw it in her face type shit,

00:27:21.616 --> 00:27:23.976
but I mean, I have daughters too.

00:27:23.976 --> 00:27:27.838
And I'm very, very
over-protective with my daughters.

00:27:27.838 --> 00:27:30.458
Like, nobody can come near them,

00:27:30.458 --> 00:27:32.348
no friends could come to the house.

00:27:32.348 --> 00:27:33.506
I have an older son.

00:27:33.506 --> 00:27:35.721
He's about to be 17.

00:27:35.721 --> 00:27:37.327
He couldn't bring his friends to the house

00:27:37.327 --> 00:27:38.974
because I had little girls, you know?

00:27:38.974 --> 00:27:40.201
And it's shit like that

00:27:40.201 --> 00:27:43.187
that you think every mother would do

00:27:43.187 --> 00:27:45.937
to make sure that their
daughters are protected.

00:27:45.937 --> 00:27:47.751
And so that's what I
did with my daughters.

00:27:47.751 --> 00:27:50.027
And I just feel like that was one part

00:27:50.027 --> 00:27:52.056
that she failed to do.

00:27:52.056 --> 00:27:53.306
So I just kinda felt like,

00:27:53.306 --> 00:27:55.086
well, why are you so like,

00:27:55.086 --> 00:27:56.186
you know, why are you crying about it,

00:27:56.186 --> 00:27:57.715
why are you making it seem
like it's a big ass deal

00:27:57.715 --> 00:28:00.737
when you put us in that
situation, you know?

00:28:00.737 --> 00:28:01.788
It's like, so yeah,

00:28:01.788 --> 00:28:03.621
It's kinda just been real iffy,

00:28:03.621 --> 00:28:06.048
but that's also one of the consequences

00:28:06.048 --> 00:28:08.666
of what I put my kids through.

00:28:08.666 --> 00:28:13.477
My son is about to be 17
and he's right now in jail.

00:28:13.477 --> 00:28:14.996
When I went to jail,

00:28:14.996 --> 00:28:18.586
he kind of left the fucking foster system.

00:28:18.586 --> 00:28:20.353
He started running away,

00:28:20.353 --> 00:28:25.156
started pretty much doing
everything that he seen me do.

00:28:25.156 --> 00:28:29.489
Robbing, stealing, doing
shit, hurting other people.

00:28:32.096 --> 00:28:34.346
And when I got out of jail,

00:28:36.526 --> 00:28:41.342
his father actually got out
a couple of months later,

00:28:41.342 --> 00:28:43.509
the one that had 20 years.

00:28:45.600 --> 00:28:47.536
And we had children's court.

00:28:47.536 --> 00:28:50.766
And I remember I was talking
to my son's grandmother,

00:28:50.766 --> 00:28:51.649
and I was like, you know,

00:28:51.649 --> 00:28:53.106
is junior gonna come by or whatever?

00:28:53.106 --> 00:28:53.939
Like, is he going to court?

00:28:53.939 --> 00:28:55.049
And she was like, no.

00:28:55.049 --> 00:28:56.106
So when I'm there,

00:28:56.106 --> 00:28:56.998
I'm talking to my attorney,

00:28:56.998 --> 00:28:58.506
and I turned and I see,

00:28:58.506 --> 00:29:01.196
I could have swore it was
my son standing right there.

00:29:01.196 --> 00:29:02.933
And I did like a little quick double-take

00:29:02.933 --> 00:29:05.247
and I mean, I thought it was my son.

00:29:05.247 --> 00:29:07.762
And I looked, and you
know, it was baby daddy.

00:29:07.762 --> 00:29:09.982
And I was like, oh shit.

00:29:09.982 --> 00:29:13.149
And I hadn't seen him in 15, 16 years.

00:29:14.391 --> 00:29:16.058
He was one of those,

00:29:16.906 --> 00:29:18.066
obviously, my first love,

00:29:18.066 --> 00:29:20.460
what I thought was love.

00:29:20.460 --> 00:29:23.681
First person I had ever been with.

00:29:23.681 --> 00:29:24.616
It was one of those

00:29:24.616 --> 00:29:26.713
like I never wanted
kids with different guys

00:29:26.713 --> 00:29:28.934
so I was willing to put up with whatever.

00:29:28.934 --> 00:29:30.916
Well, whatever our relationship
was gonna turn out to be,

00:29:30.916 --> 00:29:33.037
I was willing to go with it

00:29:33.037 --> 00:29:35.896
so that it would just be us, you know?

00:29:35.896 --> 00:29:40.557
And I remember his trial went
on for like a year or two

00:29:40.557 --> 00:29:43.480
and I was still living with his parents.

00:29:43.480 --> 00:29:45.046
But it was everyday like,

00:29:45.046 --> 00:29:46.396
you're doing this, you're cheating on me.

00:29:46.396 --> 00:29:47.229
Nobody's gonna love you.

00:29:47.229 --> 00:29:48.571
Nobody's gonna want you
'cause you have kids.

00:29:48.571 --> 00:29:49.706
Like, it was so much.

00:29:49.706 --> 00:29:51.206
I was like crying every day.

00:29:51.206 --> 00:29:52.826
And then once the year was up,

00:29:52.826 --> 00:29:53.659
I was like, you know what?

00:29:53.659 --> 00:29:54.492
I'm gone.

00:29:54.492 --> 00:29:55.720
Like, I'm the only one
taking care of our son.

00:29:55.720 --> 00:29:57.836
I would never ask his parents for nothing.

00:29:57.836 --> 00:29:58.669
I never asked them for nothing.

00:29:58.669 --> 00:30:01.081
They never paid for nothing.

00:30:01.081 --> 00:30:02.836
I would get up everyday, go to school.

00:30:02.836 --> 00:30:04.123
I would walk to school or take the bus.

00:30:04.123 --> 00:30:05.221
I never asked them for shit

00:30:05.221 --> 00:30:07.686
even though I was living at their house.

00:30:07.686 --> 00:30:10.766
But I paid for babysitting,
I paid for everything.

00:30:10.766 --> 00:30:12.075
There was nothing I asked.

00:30:12.075 --> 00:30:13.566
So when that year came up,

00:30:13.566 --> 00:30:15.020
